What is bitcoin? How does it work?
Bitcoin is a digital currency. It is a peer-to-peer payment network that is powered by its users with no central authority or banks.
Bitcoin uses cryptography to control the creation of bitcoins, to prove the ownership of bitcoins, and to control the transfer of bitcoins.
Bitcoin is created by a process called mining. Bitcoin miners solve complex math problems to be the first to create a block. A block is a group of transactions. Miners also secure the network and process transactions by running a copy of the bitcoin software and keeping the network synchronized.
